course: dictionary
lesson: 10028
title: Many meanings of tense
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have several meanings. Tense can describe a person, a muscle, a film scene or a verb. The words around it show you which meaning to use, so read the context first.
explain: «A cliffhanger ends a chapter or episode at a tense moment, so the reader must read on.» Here tense means full of suspense. Check by swapping in another word: a nervous moment or an exciting moment still fits, so you have the right meaning.
explain: Tense can also mean stretched tight, not relaxed, as in tense muscles. In grammar, tense is the form of a verb that shows time: past, present or future. Sorting out which meaning fits is easier when you look at the words around it.
fact: Tense can be an adjective, a verb or a noun in grammar.
fact: «Tense» means nervous, worried and unable to relax.
fact: «Tense» means stretched tight, not relaxed, like tense muscles.
fact: In grammar, a tense shows time: past (I walked), present (I walk) or future (I will walk).
fact: Stories are usually written in the past tense and should not jump between tenses.
exercise: «A cliffhanger ends a chapter at a tense moment, so the reader must read on.» What does tense mean here? | Cold and wet | *Full of suspense, so you feel nervous and want to know more | Stretched tight like a rope | Very sleepy and bored
exercise: Ella says, «I felt tense before my spelling test.» What does tense mean? | Relaxed and happy | Stretched tight, like a guitar string | Full of energy after a long run | *Nervous and worried, unable to relax
exercise: In «I will walk home tomorrow», which tense is "will walk"? | Past | *Future | Present | Tense is not a word that can be used here
test: «The dog's stiff, high tail showed it was tense and ready to act.» What does tense mean here? | Slow and soft | *Nervous and ready to act | Happy and playful | Relaxed and sleepy
test: «Reading your work aloud helps you hear tense slips.» In a tense slip, what goes wrong? | *The verb shows the wrong time | The spelling of a word | A missing full stop | The words are in the wrong order
exam: Which way to calm worry is shown in the lessons? | Eat a big meal quickly | Shout loudly to let it out | Tense your muscles and hold your breath | *Relax tense muscles and breathe slowly
